{
  "id": "Compound::DB00240 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Alclometasone, a corticosteroid hormone receptor agonist, is linked to Cyp3a4 through a series of molecular interactions involving glucocorticoids. The evidence suggests that Alclometasone, as part of the corticosteroid hormone receptor agonist class, binds to glucocorticoid receptors, which in turn may influence the expression or activity of Cyp3a4. This is supported by the fact that multiple corticosteroid hormones, such as cortisone acetate, fluorometholone, and budesonide, all bind to Cyp3a4, indicating a common mechanism of action involving the cytochrome P450 family, specifically Cyp3a4. The lowest common ancestors of these entities—Therapeutic Glucocorticoid and Tertiary Alpha-Hydroxy Ketone—suggest a broader pathway where glucocorticoids interact with metabolic enzymes like Cyp3a4. The consistent presence of this relationship across different corticosteroid agonists implies that the interaction between Alclometasone and Cyp3a4 is likely mediated through a shared regulatory mechanism, possibly involving receptor activation or metabolic enzyme induction.",
